# Copy to /etc/sudoers.d/haksan-ops only after reviewing paths and ownership.
# Do not use broad rules such as:
#   haksan-ops ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL
#
# Safer default: run the ops services as the same locked-down deploy user that
# already owns the Docker Compose workflow, or put haksan-ops in the docker group
# only if you accept that Docker socket access is effectively root-equivalent.
#
# If sudo is unavoidable, keep it to the audited single entry point:
# haksan-ops ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /opt/haksan/ops/bin/run-action.sh diagnostics *
# haksan-ops ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /opt/haksan/ops/bin/run-action.sh smoke_test *
# haksan-ops ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /opt/haksan/ops/bin/run-action.sh nginx_test *
# haksan-ops ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /opt/haksan/ops/bin/run-action.sh nginx_reload *
# haksan-ops ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /opt/haksan/ops/bin/run-action.sh restart_nginx *
# haksan-ops ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /opt/haksan/ops/bin/run-action.sh restart_api *
# haksan-ops ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /opt/haksan/ops/bin/run-action.sh backup_verify *
